\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{It turns out that the converse is also true: if #{F_n} is even, then #{n} must be a multiple of three.  Showing this is left as a challenge for the reader! (\em{Hint}: prove the contrapositive; if #{n} is not a multiple of three then it must be of the form #{3k+1} or #{3k+2} for some natural number #{k}.)}
